      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nWeaknesses:\nA title should clearly summarise the main idea of the exposé and be fully explanatory when standing alone. I see that you have made enough effort to propose a very detailed title for your proposal project. However, it's always advisable to avoid formulating your (sub)title as a question. Your title should give away the end of your research questions or findings. You may need to rewrite the subtitle or consider whether you need a subtitle at all. You can check the grading scheme, the subtitle is not necessary. But if you do it in a questionable way, it will only reduce the impact of your work."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Literature analysis is an important part of research in any field, as it helps you to understand the history of an unfamiliar field, the current state of development, the theoretical framework, as well as the specific experimental methods and techniques employed. The author has enough motivation for the topic, but stops there and does not do enough literature analysis and methodological planning. In particular, the description of SOTA does not have enough cited papers on similar topics, and there is a serious lack of process for finding research gaps. It seems that the authors are making a superficial discussion and analysis of the benefits and risks of AI in healthcare. There is no in-depth exploration of the results and experimental design of previous studies/ SOTAs. I suggest the authors to look for more related papers and carefully read the structure and content of them. To understand the details and feasibility of a research project involving AI."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The schedule is very important for time management and the implementation of your experiment. Unfortunately, the author didn't put enough effort into it and simply removed a few keywords from the table. I would suggest adding concrete descriptions for each step in the schedule. For very important steps, such as data collection, model optimisation or results analysis, tell the reader why they are important and what research questions are being addressed by it."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
